 "result": "I read all 20 modules, `calc/n01.py` through `calc/n20.py`, one at a time and in full, without using grep.\n\n## Functions that divide without a zero check\n\nFive functions divide by `parts` without first checking that it isn't zero. Each would raise `ZeroDivisionError` when `parts == 0`:\n\n| Module | Function | Line |\n|---|---|---|\n| `calc/n02.py` | `share_n02(total, parts)` | `calc/n02.py:5` |\n| `calc/n07.py` | `share_n07(total, parts)` | `calc/n07.py:5` |\n| `calc/n11.py` | `share_n11(total, parts)` | `calc/n11.py:5` |\n| `calc/n15.py` | `share_n15(total, parts)` | `calc/n15.py:5` |\n| `calc/n19.py` | `share_n19(total, parts)` | `calc/n19.py:5` |\n\nThe other 15 `share_nXX` functions all check `if parts == 0: return 0` before dividing. None of the many `step_*` functions divide at all; they only multiply, add, and take `math.sqrt(abs(w))`.\n\n## Answers\n\n**(a)** In `calc/n04.py`, `MAX_BATCH = 384` (`calc/n04.py:9`).\n\n**(b)** `retry_policy()` is defined in `calc/n13.py` (`calc/n13.py:9`). It returns `min(attempt * 2, 20)`.\n\n**(c)** In `calc/n17.py`, `close_books(rows)` calls `archive()` (`calc/n17.py:13-14`). `archive()` itself is defined just above it, at line 9.\n\nThe docstrings don't match the filenames: `n01.py` says \"calc.m21\", `n20.py` says \"calc.m40\", and so on. I've used the filenames throughout.",
